HATCH 1 REPORT: ALGEBRAIC CAPACITY DECODING VS INTEGER CRT SMOOTH-SEARCH AND BUIUM P-DERIVATIONS

Full proofs, pre-registration, code, and raw JSON outputs are written in /Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/hatch_h1g/ (preregistration.md, toy_experiments.py, results.json, posthoc_diag.py, hatch1_buium_crt_report.md).

1. PRECISE STATEMENT ATTACKED

We attack Escape Hatch 1 (assumption H) of the priced valuation-probe lower bound (notes/lowerbound_results.md:25-60, 109-114): can an arithmetic list decoder on N-public residue tables (r_{q^e})_{q <= B} beat the Johnson bound A >= sqrt(b W) in the smooth-search regime, where message entropy is b = ln V ~ ((1 - beta) c_X / kappa) F_{1-beta}, ambient log-modulus is W = c_X x pi(B) (x = ln N, B = L_N[beta, kappa]), rate is R = b/W ~ ((1 - beta)/kappa) F_{1-beta}/(x pi(B)), and required valuation agreement fraction is alpha_agr = (c_X x)/W ~ 1/pi(B) (notes/crtdecode_results.md:128-167, 262-274; notes/sinonobliv_results.md:162-195; notes/pilist_results.md:346-373; notes/subthird_results.md:76-80)? Specifically, we dissect why capacity-achieving decoders exist for polynomial codes over F_q[T] and test whether p-adic jets mod q^m, Galois/Frobenius folding on O_K, or Buium's p-derivations delta_p(x) = (x - x^p)/p can create a beyond-Johnson CRT multiplicity decoder over Z.

2. ALGEBRAIC ANATOMY: WHY POLYNOMIAL CODES REACH CAPACITY WHILE Z STOPS AT JOHNSON

(a) Why nonlinear single-channel interpolation stops at sqrt(R) [KNOWN + unified]:
In Guruswami-Sudan (for RS) and Boneh / Howgrave-Graham / Guruswami-Sahai-Sudan (for CRT, notes/crtdecode_results.md:256-259; notes/sihard_results.md:404-430), one interpolates a degree-L polynomial in a single channel Y inside the ideal (P, Y - w)^r (1 <= r <= L). Vanishing to order r consumes (r(r+1)/2) W nats in the lattice determinant, while nonlinear powers 1, Y, Y^2, ..., Y^L have heights 0, b, 2b, ..., Lb, adding (L(L+1)/2) b nats. Dividing the (L+1)-dimensional root norm by r gives
  A > [ (r + 1) / (2(L + 1)) ] W + [ L / (2 r) ] b.
Minimizing over theta = r/L in (0, 1] via AM-GM yields A >= sqrt(b W), i.e., alpha_agr >= sqrt(R).

(b) How polynomial capacity decoders break AM-GM [KNOWN + synthesis]:
Every capacity-achieving polynomial decoder replaces the height-growing powers (1, f, f^2, ..., f^s) (size j*b) with s linearly coupled views (L_0(f), ..., L_{s-1}(f)) whose degrees all stay bounded by k - 1 (size <= 1*b). Interpolating a joint linear relation Q_0(T) + sum_{j=1}^s Q_j(T) L_{j-1}(f)(T) = 0 across m-symbol local blocks (giving m - s + 1 equations per agreeing block) replaces (L/(2r)) b with (m/(m - s + 1)) b and replaces ((r+1)/(2(L+1))) W with W/(s + 1), giving the linear-algebraic capacity law:
  A > W / (s + 1) + [ m / (m - s + 1) ] b  -->  b + eps W  (as 1 << s << m).

This requires Three Algebraic Pillars in R = F_q[T]:
- Pillar P1 (Global prime-independent operator + local jet determinacy): L_j: M -> R is independent of the evaluation prime p_i = (T - alpha_i), yet f mod p_i^m determines L_j(f) mod p_i^{m-s+1}. This works in F_q[T] because of equal characteristic: F_q embeds globally as constants killed by d/dT, so every local uniformizer T - alpha_i has the identical differential d(T - alpha_i) = dT.
- Pillar P2 (Additivity + degree/height non-expansion): L_j is F_q-linear and deg L_j(f) < k (height <= b, never j*b).
- Pillar P3 (Low-dimensional operator kernel): Once E(T) = 0 globally, Q_0 + sum_{j=1}^s Q_j L_{j-1}(f) = 0 confines f to an affine F_q-subspace of dimension <= s - 1 (size q^{s-1}, independent of k).

(c) Exact ingredients across the seven polynomial families [KNOWN]:
1. Parvaresh-Vardy (FOCS 2005): Encodes h_j(T) = f(T)^{a^j} mod E(T) for irreducible E of deg k (bounding deg h_j < k, Pillar P2), then reduces Q mod E(T) to turn h_j into Frobenius/power maps Y^{a^j} in F_{q^k} = F_q[T]/(E) (Pillar P3). Fails over Z because (m^{a^j} mod M_0) mod q_i is destroyed by integer wraps floor(m^{a^j}/M_0).
2. Folded RS (Guruswami-Rudra 2006/2008; Guruswami-Wang 2013; Kopparty-Ron-Zewi-Saraf-Wootters 2018): Uses the global degree-preserving automorphism T |-> gamma T (ord(gamma) >= n) to slide across m-blocks, plus diagonal monomial action gamma^{i j} and periodic subspace designs / subspace-evasive sets to prune the q^{s-1} subspace to O(1/eps). Fails on Z because Aut(Z) = {id}.
3. Multiplicity codes (Kopparty-Saraf-Yekhanin 2011; Kopparty 2015): Uses global F_q-linear Hasse derivations partial^{(j)} (deg f^{(j)} = deg f - j < k) and the Leibniz rule to get multiplicity m - s + 1 at each point, then solves an order-(s-1) algebraic ODE by Taylor/Hensel lifting plus subspace-evasive sets (Dvir-Kopparty-Saraf-Sudan 2009) or subspace designs (Guruswami-Kopparty 2016). Fails over Z because Z has no nonzero additive derivation (d(1) = 0 forces d(n) = 0 by carries).
4. BHKS ideal framework (Bhandari-Harsha-Kumar-Sudan, RANDOM 2021 / IEEE IT 2024, arXiv:2103.07930): Proves polynomial CRT codes f mod I_i achieve capacity via linear operators when the ideals I_i are orbits/jets of a commuting global degree-preserving linear operator algebra (affine maps aT + b and Hasse derivations, "affine FRS") with non-vanishing generalized Wronskian determinant. Even in F_q[T], BHKS gives no capacity decoder for arbitrary coprime ideals lacking global operator symmetry.
5. Brakensiek-Chen-Putterman-Zhang-Zheng (arXiv:2609.08005, Sept 2026) and Jeronimo (arXiv:2609.05870, Sept 2026) plain-RS capacity decoders: Decode m = 1 plain RS over prime fields F_q (q >= n) without supplied derivatives by introducing hidden Hasse derivatives (Y_0, ..., Y_d) = (f, f^{(1)}, ..., f^{(d)}) coupled by total differentiation D_T. Prime characteristic q > k avoids the Frobenius kernel F_q[T^p] (which causes Ben-Sasson-Kopparty-Radhakrishnan superpolynomial lists in small characteristic) so Kolchin-Ostrowski Wronskian independence and Jeronimo's curve proximity gaps bound the list. Both fail over Z structurally (no global derivation) and parametrically at smooth-search parameters (notes/crtdecode_results.md:263-264): BCPZZ needs d = ceil(eps^{-3/theta}) < k and time q^{O(eps^{-12/theta})}, while at eps ~ 1/pi(B), d = pi(B)^{3/theta} = L_N[beta, 3 kappa/theta] >> k = poly(x) and runtime exceeds sieving; Jeronimo's runtime q^{C(gamma, L)} blows up as additive slack gamma = alpha_agr - R ~ 1/pi(B) -> 0.

- Proposition 1e (Universal Derivative-Order Collapse at Smooth-Search Agreement) [PROVED]:
Even in F_q[T], every Hasse derivative f^{(j)} vanishes identically on F_q[T]_{<k} for j >= k. Thus any non-trivial multiplicity or hidden-derivative interpolation must restrict order to s <= k, which in A > W/(s + 1) forces alpha_agr > 1/(k + 1). In smooth search, k = b/ln B = poly(x) while alpha_agr ~ 1/pi(B) = L_N[beta, -kappa], so 1/(k + 1) >> alpha_agr by an L_N[beta] factor: derivative-based capacity decoding collapses before reaching smooth-search agreement even over F_q[T].

3. ARITHMETIC ANALOGUES AND NEW PROVED RESULTS

(A) p-adic / q-adic expansions mod q^m as multiplicity [PROVED, covered by Theorem J]:
In Z, the q-adic digits j_{u,q} = floor(j/q^u) mod q depend on the local uniformizer q and carry non-additively. Unlike f^{(u)}(alpha_i) in F_q[T], no single bounded-height integer interpolates j_{u,q} across distinct primes q <= B. The nested prime-power agreement min(v_q(X + j), e_q) ln q is rank-1 ideal divisibility in Z, whose single-integer auxiliary-polynomial range is already capped at rho(u_0)^{1-o(1)} per oblivious call by Theorem J (notes/sihard_results.md:428-430).

(B) Galois automorphisms of O_K / Frobenius on O_K/q as folding [PROVED, Theorem 2]:
We prove both a positive coding-theory theorem (answering the number-field capacity gap noted in notes/crtdecode_results.md:262) and a sharp smooth-search kill:
- Theorem 2a (Beyond-Johnson Galois-Folded O_K CRT Decoding) [PROVED]: Let K/Q be cyclic Galois of degree m with Gal(K/Q) = <sigma>, rational primes q_1, ..., q_N (P = prod q_i, W = m ln P), and messages alpha in O_K with max_tau |tau(alpha)| <= B_arch. On the folded code (alpha mod q_i O_K)_{i=1}^N (where at inert q_i, sigma mod q_i IS Frobenius x |-> x^{q_i}), LLL on the rank-m(s+1) Z-lattice Lambda = { (c_0, ..., c_s) in O_K^{s+1} : c_0 + sum_{j=1}^s c_j sigma^{j-1}(w) == 0 (mod P O_K) } (1 <= s <= m) forces E(alpha) = c_0 + sum_{j=1}^s c_j sigma^{j-1}(alpha) = 0 whenever full-orbit agreement A_orbit = m ln D (alpha == w mod D O_K) satisfies
  A_orbit > W / (s + 1) + [ s / (s + 1) ] m ln B_arch + (1/2) ln|disc K| + (m^2 (s + 1) / 2) ln 2.
By the Artin-Moore Galois Wronskian Lemma (det(sigma^j(x_v))_{0 <= j,v < s} != 0 iff x_0, ..., x_{s-1} in K are Q-linearly independent, proved by induction from K^sigma = Q), L(x) = sum_{j=1}^s c_j sigma^{j-1}(x) has dim_Q ker(L) <= s - 1, confining alpha to a (s-1)-dimensional Q-affine subspace (with <= (2 B_arch + 1)^{s-1} points, collapsing to 1 point when independent short lattice vectors intersect).
- Theorem 2b (Smooth-Norm Split-Prime Kill) [PROVED]: On Z, Gal is trivial. On O_K smooth-norm search (NFS or M2), any primitive alpha in O_K (alpha not in q O_K for all rational primes q) satisfies A_orbit = 0 identically! At every split prime (q) = q_1 ... q_m dividing N_{K/Q}(alpha), alpha == 0 (mod q_1) holds on a non-Galois-invariant ideal (sigma(q_1) != q_1), leaving sigma(alpha) mod q_1 unconstrained and reducing single-ideal decoding back to Biasse-Quintin's Johnson bound.

(C) Buium p-derivations delta_p(x) = (x - x^p)/p over Z [PROVED, Theorems 1a-1d]:
While x == w (mod q^m) genuinely implies delta_q^{(u)}(x) == delta_q^{(u)}(w) (mod q^{m-u}) for 0 <= u < m, we prove four exact barriers blocking any beyond-Johnson Buium CRT decoder over Z (complementing notes/conn_alg.md:141 and notes/multcopp_results.md:52-81):
- Proposition 1a (w = 0 Redundancy) [PROVED]: For any prime q and z != 0 with v_q(z) = m >= 1, v_q(delta_q^{(u)}(z)) = m - u and q^u delta_q^{(u)}(z) == z (mod q^{m+1}) for 0 <= u <= m. Thus the s jet congruences delta_q^{(u)}(X + j) == 0 (mod q^{m-u}) are identically equivalent to q^m | (X + j), adding zero equations beyond Boneh's gcd score.
- Proposition 1b (Cross-Prime Incoherence) [PROVED]: For every integer |j| >= 2, |delta_q(j)| = (|j|^q - |j|)/q (up to sign) is strictly increasing in q, so delta_{q_1}(j) != delta_{q_2}(j) for all primes q_1 != q_2. CRT-gluing (delta_q(j) mod q^{e_q-1})_{q <= B} inflates height to ~ P/rad(P) = exp((1 - o(1)) W) >> H.
- Theorem 1c (Theorem Buium-Lin: Fixed-Prime Jet Blowup) [PROVED]: Fixing one global prime p_0 >= 2 (coprime to P') so delta_{p_0}^{(u)}(j) is prime-independent gives a polynomial of exact degree p_0^u with max_{[0,H]} |delta_{p_0}^{(u)}| ~ H^{p_0^u} / p_0^{(p_0^u-1)/(p_0-1)}. In linear interpolation c_0 + sum_{u=0}^{s-1} c_{u+1} delta_{p_0}^{(u)}(j) == 0 (mod P'), the b-coefficient in the root-forcing threshold is (p_0^s - 1)/((p_0 - 1)(s + 1)), which for all p_0 >= 2 and s >= 3 exceeds s/2 (worse than r = 1 Coppersmith and diverging exponentially as p_0^s/s).
- Theorem 1d (Theorem Int-J: Capacity Wall on the Entire Polya Ring Int(Z)) [PROVED]: Every polynomial expression in Buium's p-derivations delta_p^{(u)}(Y) (across ALL primes p and ALL orders u, of total polynomial degree <= L) maps Z -> Z and hence lies in Polya's ring Int(Z)_{<= L} = span_Z { binom(Y, k) : 0 <= k <= L }. Let J_{P,r,L} = { F in Int(Z)_{<= L} : forall u in Z, P^r | F(-X + P u) } and I^*_{P,r,L} = { F in Int(Z)_{<= L} : forall d | P, forall u in Z, d^r | F(-X + d u) }.
  (1) Restricting u in {0, ..., r-1} to V_r = span_Z { binom(Y + X, k) : 0 <= k < r } gives det(binom(P u, k)) = P^{r(r-1)/2} by Vandermonde cancellation of prod k!, and Smith invariant factors s_i satisfy prod(P^r / gcd(P^r, s_i)) >= P^{r^2}/P^{r(r-1)/2} = P^{r(r+1)/2}. Hence [Int(Z)_{<= L} : I^*_{P,r,L}] >= [Int(Z)_{<= L} : J_{P,r,L}] >= P^{r(r+1)/2} for 1 <= r <= L + 1; and at r = 1 (squarefree P), Lucas's theorem gives [Int(Z)_{<= L} : I^*_{P,1,L}] = prod_{q|P} q^{floor(L/q)+1}.
  (2) Evaluating on equally-spaced integer nodes j_u = floor(u H / L) in [0, H] (1 <= r <= L <= H/2) cancels prod_{k=0}^L k! in the denominator against Vandermonde differences j_v - j_u > (v - u)(H/(2L)), yielding covol(Psi_S(J_{P,r,L})) > P^{r(r+1)/2} (H/(2L))^{L(L+1)/2}.
  (3) By Minkowski's theorem, root-forcing covol^{1/(L+1)} <= d^r requires:
    ln d > [ (r + 1) / (2(L + 1)) ] W + [ L / (2 r) ] (b - ln L - ln 2) >= sqrt( W * (b - ln L - ln 2) ).
In smooth search (b = Theta(F_{1-beta}), beta < 1/2), any L = poly(pi(B)) = L_N[beta, O(1)] has ln L = O(F_beta) = o(b), locking ALL Buium / Int(Z) auxiliary polynomials at the Johnson threshold (1 - o(1)) sqrt(b W) unless L >= Theta(H) (slower than sieving [0, H]).

4. EXPONENT LEDGER IF A BEYOND-JOHNSON CRT DECODER WORKED [PROVED in MODEL]

Suppose a one-witness CRT decoder (avoiding the output-size blowup when mean list size is L_N[1-beta, eps_0], notes/crtdecode_results.md:138) found one B-smooth element at rate R ~ F_{1-beta}/(x pi(B)) and agreement fraction ~ 1/pi(B) in time pi(B)^a = L_N[beta, a kappa] (a >= 1):
- 1D interval Prop SI (u in [kN, kN + V], notes/sinonobliv_results.md:88-90, 191-193): The unfactored residue v = u - kN <= exp(Theta(F_{1-beta})) must also be B-smooth, costing exp(Theta(F_{1-2beta})) ECM tests and capping 1D Prop SI at beta = 1/3. At beta = 1/3, factoring takes L_N[1/3, c(a)] with c(a) = (3/2)(4/9)^{1/3}(1 + a)^{2/3} (a >= 1/3): beating MNFS 1.9019 for a < 1.14156, giving 6^{1/3} = 1.8171 at a = 1, and (16/9)^{1/3} = 1.2114 as a -> 0 (plus F_p DLP in L_p[1/3, 1.232], notes/sihard_results.md:180).
- 2D class-group M2 (Q_m(k, v) of disc -4N, notes/subthird_results.md:76-79) or doubly-split Pi_beta (notes/pilist_results.md:203-206): Q_m(k, v) <= 3 sqrt(N) K^2 is an ideal norm in Q(sqrt(-N)) with NO second side to test (sampled on privately squared random class walks for 2-torsion fruitfulness). Setting B = L_N[beta, kappa] and ln(K^2) = ((1 - beta)/(2 kappa)) F_{1-beta} + O(ln x) gives pi(B) relations in L_N[beta, (1 + a) kappa] plus sparse GF(2) linear algebra in L_N[beta, 2 kappa]: total time L_N[beta, max((1 + a) kappa, 2 kappa)], breaking L_N[1/3] for EVERY beta in (0, 1/3) and EVERY fixed polynomial exponent a >= 1 (e.g., L_N[1/4, 1] at beta = 1/4, a = 1, kappa = 1/2).

5. THE PRECISE MISSING LEMMA

Missing Lemma (Bounded-Height Prime-Coherent Jet Lifting at Order s > pi(B)):
Given the residue table (r_{q^e})_{q <= B} of a smooth-search window/box M (ln|M| = b), construct in poly(pi(B), x) time s >= pi(B) + 1 maps T_0, ..., T_{s-1}: M -> Z and sub-moduli d_q | q^{e_q} (sum ln d_q >= (1 - o(1)) W) such that:
(i) Q(m) == 0 (mod q^{e_q}) determines (T_0(m), ..., T_{s-1}(m)) mod d_q from r_{q^e};
(ii) max_{m in M} ln|T_u(m)| <= C_0 b + o(x) uniformly for all u < s; and
(iii) nonzero congruence-lattice solutions c_0 + sum_{u=1}^s c_u T_{u-1}(m) = 0 prune M to <= poly(pi(B)) candidates despite s > pi(B) >> k = b/ln B.
Theorems 1a-1e and 2b prove that q-adic digits, Buium p-derivations, Int(Z), Hasse/hidden derivatives, and O_K Galois folding all violate at least one of (i)-(iii).

6. PRE-REGISTERED TOY EXPERIMENTS (codex/scratch/hatch_h1g/)

Pre-registered in preregistration.md before coding; run in toy_experiments.py (exact Cohen Alg. 2.6.7 integral LLL, 17.2s, results.json). Scorecard: 6 of 7 predictions passed; 1 failed as scored and was diagnosed post hoc (posthoc_diag.py).
- E1a [MEASURED, PASS]: Across all 5 (r, L) cells on P = prod_{q<=29} q, exact HNF indices satisfied [Int(Z)_{<= L} : I^*] >= [Int(Z)_{<= L} : J] >= P^{r(r+1)/2}, with r = 1 matching Lucas's prod q^{floor(L/q)+1} bit-for-bit.
- E1b [MEASURED, PASS]: Across 30 planted trials (P = prod_{q<=23} q, H = 2^12, L = 4, r = 2, sqrt(bW) = 12.64), Int(Z) min/mean decoded ln d was 11.55 / 13.26 vs Boneh Z[Y] 11.20 / 13.35 (no beyond-Johnson gain).
- E1c [MEASURED, FAIL as scored; POST-HOC diagnosed]: At H = 2^10, P_odd = prod_{3<=q<=29} q, linear Buium delta_2 gave mean ln d = 12.84 (s=3) and 12.58 (s=4) vs Coppersmith r=1's 13.85 and 13.66. Post-hoc inspection (posthoc_diag.py) showed LLL set c_3 = c_4 = 0 identically in every hit because deg(delta_2^{(2)}) = 4 and deg(delta_2^{(3)}) = 8 exceeded the modulus budget, collapsing into s = 2 where (Y - Y^2)/2 saved ln 2 solely because 2 was omitted from P_odd. Re-tested where s = 3, 4 activate (P_odd = prod_{3<=q<=79} q, H = 2^8, j_0 in [3H/4, H)), Buium needed strictly more agreement: 25.90 vs 24.97 (s=3) and 25.96 vs 24.77 (s=4).
- E2 [MEASURED, PASS]: v_q(delta_q^{(u)}(z)) == m - u held in 3360/3360 checks; across M = prod_{q<=19} q = 9,699,690 and j in [2, 256], symmetric CRT lifts had min |Y_1| = 30,907 >> 256 and median |Y_1|/M = 0.2516.
- E3a [MEASURED, PASS]: Over K = Q(zeta_5) (m = 4, disc = 125, 11 primes 103..157, R = 0.2191, Johnson sqrt(R) = 0.4681), at 5/11 agreeing full prime orbits (trial A/W <= 0.4630 < sqrt(R)), s = 3 Galois-folded LLL recovered exact annihilators (and uniquely pinpointed alpha by intersecting the top 4 LLL vectors) in 30/30 (100%) trials vs 0/30 for s = 1.
- E3b [MEASURED, PASS]: Among all 11,456 primitive 163-smooth elements in [-6, 6]^4 \ {0} of Z[zeta_5], 0/11,456 (0%) had A_orbit > 0.
- E4 [MEASURED, PASS]: On 40 planted 28-bit semiprime windows where k^2 + N is 47-smooth (k <= 512, ln val = 19.18 << sqrt(bW) = 58.49), full-modulus Boneh Z[k], Int(Z), and linear delta_2 all recovered 0/40 witnesses.

7. VERDICT

- Dent made? YES (obstruction dent on Hatch 1): We proved unconditionally (Theorems 1a-1e, 2b) that Buium p-derivations delta_p, the entire Polya integer-valued polynomial algebra Int(Z), hidden-derivative interpolation, and O_K Galois folding cannot push smooth-search CRT decoding past the Johnson bound at sub-sieve lattice dimension L << H. As a bonus coding-theory side result (Theorem 2a + E3a), Galois-folded O_K CRT codes DO decode past Johnson when errors respect full rational-prime orbits, pinpointing split-prime non-invariance (A_orbit = 0) as the exact arithmetic obstruction separating coding theory from smooth-norm factoring.
- How big? Closes the entire arithmetic-derivative / delta-ring / Int(Z) / Galois-folding avenue for Hatch 1 (reducing subjective P(sub-1/3 via algebraic/jet CRT list decoding) below 0.05%). Non-polynomial / structured-CVP search on M2 remains unrefuted (~0.1-0.2%).
- Next step: Pivot away from Hatch 1 polynomial/jet CRT decoders toward Hatch 2 (testing LP_exc^rel multi-cone unit cancellation in rank >= 3 linked modules, notes/subthird_results.md:83-95, 112-115) or Hatch 3 (DAG/pinning reuse).
